      "content": "but there is no \"self\" here now. that's the thing. everything i did—every meal i cooked, every medicine i gave, every night i stayed awake—it was all for her. without that, there isn't even a foundation to build on. it's like looking into a mirror and seeing nothing. it's not that i'm \"adjusting,\" it's that the purpose of my entire existence has been erased. how am i supposed to care about \"the immediate present\" when the present has no meaning? it just feels like waiting for nothing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
